l give you varying  attributes depending on what crystal  tiers you equip to it  you'll also be able to upgrade how many  estus flask uses you get by using  special golden seeds if you recall from  the game's trailer there are giant  golden herb trees throughout the game  that are clearly significant there are  also smaller lesser earth trees you can  find throughout the game's map at these  lesser earth trees you'll find special  golden seas which are exactly what you  need to upgrade your estus flask uses  the number of seeds you need will change  as you upgrade your flask and this isn't  the only way to obtain these seeds  additionally you can upgrade the  recovery strength of your estus flasks  back to sites of grace though as the  game is now open world these act like  bonfires from dark souls 2 or 3 and that  you can immediately warp to them once  you've activated them unlike those games  so long as you're not in battle you can  warp to any sight of grace at pretty  much any point in time  the map and world of alden ring is  absolutely massive so these are meant to  not only be a spot of respite but an  important way to quickly travel around  the map  however that means the map could quickly  become overrun with a ridiculous number  of sites of grace every time you enter a  legacy dungeon or smaller dungeon in  order to account for this you'll find  several stakes of america throughout the  game  think of these like mini checkpoints you  can't rest at them like a site of grace  nor can you manage some of your special  equipment here  however if you die you can choose to  return to life at either a nearby state  of america or site of grace this allows  from software to play stakes of america  in ways where you won't have to  tediously backtrack from various sites  of grace if you die and they also won't  need to overpopulate the map with too  many warpable sites of grace  and speaking of death the game works  just like previous soulsborne games and  how it's handled there are no save  points in eldon ring and the game is  consistently auto saving  upon death instead of needing to load a  prior save you'll lose all of your  currency and respawn at your nearest  checkpoint you'll have a chance to  regain this lost currency but should you  die again that currency is permanently  lost in eldon ring this currency is  referred to as runes runes are what  you'll be using to not only purchase  items and weapons in the game but are  also your experience points you'll be  using to level up  on top of purchasing weapons you can use  your runes to upgrade your weapons and  make them more powerful this mechanic is  just like previous games you'll find  various blacksmiths around the lands  between who can upgrade your weapons  with a number of runes and certain rare  upgrade materials  weapon upgrades not only raise their  basic attack power but can also affect  their attribute scaling you can find  these on every weapon under the  attribute scaling section of the menu if  there's a letter next to a stat like a d  next to strength it means that your  weapon has extra bonus damage based on  how good the letter is and how high your  strength stat is  again like prior from software games  various weapons will require certain  attributes in order to be able to use  them in the first place  so that means the best weapon for you  will very much depend on what build  you're using  equip load is also back which means the  heavier the armor and weapons you're  using the slower your character will  move and the less invincibility frames  they'll have when attempting to dodge  away from enemies  new to eldon ring is crafting around the  lands between you'll find various  crafting materials out in the wilderness  and even from slaying various creatures  you'll find roaming about the items you  can craft range from being able to cure  status ailments like poison deposits or  knives you can throw at enemies or even  to crafting special arrows to use with a  bow tated with crafting you'll also be  able to find and or purchase various  cookbooks which will teach the player  how to craft more advanced items  something i've brought up multiple times  at this point is the world map which is  new to alden ring as the game is open  world and the map is so much more  massive than previous souls games from  software has added a map with the  ability to fast travel at certain points  however if you're not the biggest fan of  this edition you don't have to worry too  much as the map is very basic while it  does show the wider world you can use it  to find some points of interest and npcs  may even mark points of interest on the  map the game's smaller dungeons stirring  throughout the world and legacy dungeons  have no maps associated with them so  you'll still have to figure out how to  navigate through those mazes on your own  without the aid of this tool  additionally you don't start off with a  map but rather we'll have to find map  fragments in order to slowly fill it in  yourself  and speaking of dungeons from software  has completely changed how they've  approached the overall map design to  eldon ring in order to create something  open world once you enter the game's  first area in limgrave the map will  immediately open up to you so you won't  have an extremely guided experience and  interwoven map like we've seen in games  like bloodborne or dark souls 1.  however within the lands between you'll  discover both hidden dungeons and legacy  dungeons the hidden dungeons act like  mini dungeons and even though they're  small are little tastes of that classic  from software level design some of these  dungeons are easy to find some are  hidden behind walls you'll need to leap  over and some of them can be found next  to the guidance of statues you'll find  in the world that will help indicate  what direction to go  many of these dungeons are slightly  reminiscent of chalice dungeons from  bloodborne in their scale but unlike  those they're all handcrafted and well  thought out however there are also  larger dungeons you'll find that aren't  legacy dungeons so the size and scope  widely varies  meanwhile the game's legacy dungeons are  similar to major from software areas of  the past  in a way you can think of it like  stumbling upon an area from demon souls  instead of returning to a hub to access  boletaria or separately latria now  you'll be able to travel across an open  world that connects bolotario to latria  or perhaps more on the scale of finding  irithyll the boreal valley from dark  souls 3. the legacy dungeons themselves  are large interwoven and intricately  designed with plenty of verticality and  uniqueness and will give you that  classic from software experience i'm  sure you're craving if you're a fan of  these games  in order to help traverse the world  you'll now have a spectral steed called  torrent who you can summon at any point  in time as long as you're outside of  dungeons and legacy dungeons with a  spectral steed whistle  riding horseback is its own unique  experience in eldon ring all of your  weapons have unique movesets for riding  horseback with some like lance's meant  for this type of combat your horse can  also double jump and utilize spirit  springs to launch up high in the air and  access areas much higher than a double  jump can  there are also bosses you'll find in the  field designed to be fought via  horseback as opposed to on foot while  playing the network test i came across a  tree sentinel boss early on one time i  tackled and defeated him on foot while  another i attempted to fight horseback  while it was certainly possible to do  the fight on foot the battle was far  easier on horseback and this was  definitely meant to be the way to tackle  this particular boss you'll also  encounter a dragon that was shown in the  elder ring trailers and once again this  boss is definitely easier to tackle on  your steed  all of that said as you can't bring your  steed into dungeons this in no way  replaces traditional souls combat but  rather is an additional experience on  top of that classic from software style  gameplay  while the lands between are entirely  connected at least as far as we're  currently aware there is a central hub  similar to firelink shrine majula or the  hunter's dream and you'll find plenty to  do within the hub which is completely  separate from the open world of the game  again as far as we're aware  if you're familiar with prior from  software games you'll have a good grasp  of how combat works it'll have both an  hp and fp meter with fp allowing you to  perform magic and special weapon attacks  you'll also have a stamina meter which  is crucial to these games as you'll need  to wait for it to recharge before you  can perform actions like attacking or  dodging  you'll have four basic sets of moves per  weapon and shield with each weapon you  can use it one-handed with a set of  light attacks or heavier attacks or  choose to dual-wield your weapon for a  separate set of more powerful light and  heavy attacks  you can equip your shields or weapons to  any hand you like meaning if you want  you can wield two weapons at once and  sometimes combine these attacks at the  expense of more defense  each weapon and shield come with the  type of weapon art some of these weapons  are locked per weapon especially when it  comes to unique weapons however you'll  also find many equippable weapon arts as  you play through the game which you'll  be able to equip to non-unique weapons  similar to previous soulsborne games  you'll also be able to parry enemy  attacks opening them up for a much more  powerful repost similarly you can strafe  around your enemies to try and find an  opening to backstab them  new to elden ring are guard counters by  blocking an enemy attack you can  immediately counter with a strong guard  counter that can break the stance of  many stubborn opponents  however it comes with the risk of being  relatively slow so perform these at your  own risk  also new to elden ring are two abilities  carried over from seikiro you'll now be  able to use stealth to sneak around  enemies as well as jump these elements  have worked their way into combat as you  can use stealth to sneak up to enemies  without alerting them to quickly  backstab them or at the very least take  them out before they can call for  reinforcements  meanwhile you can attack while jumping  with these attacks also being a good way  to break enemies guards it also allows  you to reach and attack potential weak  points of certain opponents  outside of melee combat range combat has  returned with various caster builds and  spells you can utilize  to be honest i didn't play around with  these as much as the melee builds so i  don't know quite as much about it but it  seems to act just like prior games with  plenty of amazing spells you'll find  throughout the game  something brand new to elden ring are  spirit ashes you can equip these ashes  in the same slot as your esses flasks  and use them to summon spirits who will  help attack enemies and bosses  in my experience finding spirit ashes  you could equip was like finding any  other weapon or armor with some hidden  away and others available for purchase  from merchants the spirit ashes are  meant to be an additional way players  can tackle challenges and thereby make  the game more accessible to a larger  group of players  while one critique of the game has been  that the spirit ashes make it too easy  especially after people had a chance to  use them in the network test according  to a game informer who played the closed  beta early these summons have been  severely nerfed and hardly do anything  against major bosses  like weapons however you'll be able to  find a special spirit tuner who it seems  like will be able to upgrade the power  of your spirit ashes meaning it's  another thing that from software has  tried to balance into the game with  upgrades  something interesting that was  implemented in the closed beta was that  for defeating certain bosses in this  case market from the trailer and network  test players now receive a talisman slot  talismans act as your special attribute  rings in elden ring as of now it's  unclear how many of these slots you'll  be able to unlock but it's definitely  interesting you currently had to defeat  a boss in order to do so  like demon souls dark souls and  bloodborne alden ring will feature an  always online multiplayer you'll be able  to see bloodstains of other tarnish who  have perished and leave and rate  messages to help other players or try to  get them to waste their time you'll also  be able to invade other players worlds  for pvp meaning as a player who isn't  partaking that you still run the risk of  having your own world invaded by a  hostile player  but you can also summon players to help  you progress and players can be summoned  in to help with pvp  covenants will also be returning  although details on those are currently  scant  miyazaki has stated that he wants the  online multiplayer to be easier to  access than ever before and there are  now summoning pools within eldon ring in  order to make it easier to find players  looking to help or fight  and that's all i have for you today i  hope you enjoyed this i tried my best to  balance revealing important gameplay  details while also not being too  spoilery this is part of a series of  alvin ring content we're making in  preparation for the upcoming release if  you enjoyed this i'd love it if you  checked out my look back at one of my  favorite from software games kings field  and i can't wait to cover more elden  ring and go down this journey with all  you fellow tarnished

